Well, it turned to be a RAM problem. I found a set of 8MB parity SIMMs,
and the machine is stable with theses. The others one were ECC, but
I don't think this should be a problem. Both are 60ns ... strange.

Anyway I found a way to add a fan to this box: next to the PCI dauther card,
on the metal part which goes from front to back. It moves air from the disk
part to the CPU/PCI part of the box, and it seems to help. My HDs seems to
be less hot, as to the cache chips.

